an error handed through an out parameter must be autoreleased

submitIntent created the NSError owned, passed it to the user block, and released it. The block
writes it straight into the caller's NSError** without retaining, because that is the convention,
so the caller was left holding a freed object and ARC retained it the instant the call returned.
iA Writer died in objc_retain, called from -[IALibraryObserver _createDirectoryAndAddFilePresenter].

It is autoreleased at the handover, on the thread that invokes the block, because the async path
runs later on another queue and a pool from here would be long gone.

